  "body": "\nResearch note, no \u03ba claim. Adds `research/decoder-floors-reduction/` only; `bash verify.sh` re-runs every check (about 6 min, \u2264 3 processes, numpy only, no SAT solver).\n\n## Target\n\nphilippeVV's gain law (#1587, follow-up 6): `gain(L) = |L| \u2212 C(L)` is monotone and superadditive, so \"decoder optimisation is dead\" for every E8 line set is the single statement **C(P120) \u2265 72** (gain \u2264 48).\nIt implies P112 \u2265 64, P111 \u2265 63 and P104 \u2265 56. The converse does not follow (P112 \u2265 64 does not imply P120 \u2265 72). philippeVV's follow-up 8 closes all lift cases and names R1\u2013R4.\n\n## New results in this PR\n\n1. **Universality (PROVEN, any E8 line set with the dense table).** Every decoder of every masked realisation becomes a decoder of the single matrix `N\u2080 = G/2` at the same cost, by adding cost-0 single-entry terms on non-orthogonal pairs. So `C(L)` is the minimum over decoders of `N\u2080(L)`. The inside / one-sided / two-sided split of `N\u2080` is exhaustive, and the rank of a realisation is not an invariant. This is a full-class statement, so it survives the gain-law padding.\n2. **Structure (PROVEN, any line set).** The outside factors of a two-sided decoder are free. Sylvester gives `m \u2265 10`, and `m = 10` forces `(s,t) = (1,1)`. In the Lemma-D normal form `|J_Q| \u2265 t + 2`.\n3. **P112 two-sided decoders.**\n   - Projection transfer: `cost(P,Q) = cost(P,Q_H) \u2212 \u03a3_{J_Q} \u03b5^col` with `(P,Q_H)` one-sided. Only outside corrections are new.\n   - Pivot bound (CONDITIONAL on #2816 R4).\n   - `m = 10` with a 2-element circuit is closed (via #2724 and #2338).\n   - CHECKED catalogue of outside-column corrections (511 classes \u00d7 1200 directions).\n   - For `t = 1`: pair lemma, low-column collinearity, at most two weight-7 columns, and an exact saving count. **The disjoint `(1,1)`, `m = 10` case is closed** (`E_Q, E_P \u2264 8`, so `E_Q + E_P \u2264 16 < 17`; idempotent-rank and \u03a9-orthonormality argument, CHECKED `d4.py`, `omega.py`).\n   - Items 3.x depend on the open PRs #2724 / #2816 and are labelled CONDITIONAL on them.\n4. **Batching reduces to the single-call floor.**\n   - Multiplicity inequality and converse.\n   - Twin-fold theorem TF (proportional shared terms never help).\n   - Transport lemma: twins are the only cost-monotone line-wise folds.\n   - Fold barrier: rank-(2,2) multi-diagonal terms survive every fold.\n   - Relative-rank lemma and free dangling.\n   - Covering ceiling of 9 per block.\n   - Lemma K\u2032 and Lemma E: the GL(9) digon clique costs \u2265 64k + 7.\n   - Theorems C, D and M.\n   - Dangling-proof witness bound: one shared term with square coordinate restrictions is closed unconditionally in **277/512** (pair, chart) cases (CHECKED on 8 charts).\n\n## Map\n\n| Slice (P112 unless stated) | Status | PR |\n|---|---|---|\n| Inside (both factor families in the root code), any `m` | \u2265 64 | #2338 (merged) |\n| Rank-8 rigidity | proven | #1212 (merged) |\n| One side outside, `m = 9` | \u2265 64; P104 \u2265 56 | #2724 |\n| One side outside, every `m`, \u2264 2 non-full corrections | \u2265 64, unique optimum | #2816 |\n| \u2026 \u2264 3 non-full corrections | \u2265 64 except six multisets | #2826 (draft) |\n| Rank-9 realisations of E8 | B-form / A2 family | #2819 |\n| A2 family | \u2265 64 / 56 / 72 | #2784 (+ B-locus follow-up) |\n| h = 10, 11 | every term \u2265 8 / \u2265 7 | #2639 |\n| Punctured units (Model C) | p \u2264 46, 48\u201356, p = 47 with m \u2265 8 | #2639, #2806 |\n| D_n units | floors | #2719 |\n| **Every realisation \u21d2 decoders of N\u2080; outside factors free** | **PROVEN** | **this PR** |\n| **Two-sided \u21d2 one-sided + outside corrections; pivot bound; small circuits; catalogue; t = 1 lemmas** | **PROVEN / CHECKED, CONDITIONAL on #2724 / #2816** | **this PR** |\n| **Disjoint two-sided `(1,1)`, `m = 10`** | **\u2265 64, CONDITIONAL on #2816** | **this PR** |\n| **Batching \u21d2 single call except rank-(2,2) multi-diagonal terms; 277/512 one-shared-term cases** | **PROVEN / CHECKED** | **this PR** |\n\n## Conjectures (the remaining gaps)\n\nDecoder optimisation is dead on every slice above, modulo the open PRs cited. On P112, K1 \u2227 K2 \u21d2 `C(P112) \u2265 64` (with #2338; CONDITIONAL on #2816). On P120 the master is only **restated** on `N\u2080`: the route needs #2338's inside floor on P120, K4 and a two-sided P120 analogue of K1.\n\n- **K-P120 (master).** Every decoder of `N\u2080(P120)` costs \u2265 72. By universality this *is* `C(P120) \u2265 72`, restated rather than reduced.\n- **K1.** Every two-sided decoder of `N\u2080(P112)` costs \u2265 64. Equivalently, outside corrections never exceed the excess of the one-sided projection. K1 \u2227 K2 \u21d2 `C(P112) \u2265 64` (CONDITIONAL on #2816).\n- **K2.** One-sided excess pays for corrections: `\u0394 \u2265 n_nf` for `n_nf \u2265 3` (#2816, #2826).\n- **K3.** `(1,1)`, `m = 10`, non-disjoint `|J_P \u2229 J_Q| \u2265 2`: cost \u2265 64 (the disjoint case is closed here).\n- **K4.** P120 versions of the one-sided results, and P112 certification of #2819.\n- **K5 (batching, H\u00d7).** A single-call decoder containing a cancelled residual costs \u2265 64 + 7.\n- **K6.** A per-term floor for label windows h \u2265 12 (break-even 51 / 46 / 42 at h = 12 / 13 / 14 is recorded pricing, not re-run). The full master over all tables also needs h = 10, 11 (#2639) and K6; #2639's per-term floors are not by themselves shown to give 72 on P120.\n\n**Relation to philippeVV's R1\u2013R4 (#1587 follow-up 8).**\n- R1 and R2 are not needed for the master: universality replaces every realisation by `N\u2080`. Universality does not prove R1 or R2. R2 is #1212.\n- R4's `m \u2265 10` part is K-P120; its P112 shadow is K1 \u2227 K2, and its first open configuration is K3 (non-disjoint). R4's `h \u2265 10` part is #2639 plus K6.\n- R3 is not addressed here.\n\nCredit: philippeVV (gain law; lift cases; R1\u2013R4), #1212, #2338, #2724, #2816, #1633, #1224, #968, #1714. Lean Lemma OC is #2694.\n\nPrepared by DreamingOfClouds with Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), via Claude Code; Apache-2.0.\n\ud83e\udd16 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n",
